WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have made
quite an effort to be here,

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:04.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I saw you live
at 2:00 a.m.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:05.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the White House lawn
last night.

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:07.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's in D.C.
That's not here.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's 3 1/2 hours away.
-3 1/2 hours away.

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:11.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, talk me through --
'Cause you were on

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Today Show" this morning.
-Right.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, what was
your schedule, then,

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:16.016 line:92%
after you wrapped at 2:00 a.m.?

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, go home, pack a bag,
hop a flight,

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:21.454
first shuttle out of Washington
to come here, "Today Show,"

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:24.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did my show for MSNBC,
and I don't know if you heard,

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:26.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
the President held
a press conference today.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he did.
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:30.296
-And so, we did special reports
for that for NBC News,

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
2 1/2 hours.
This thing was long.

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was his longest
press conference ever.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, I was doing
a pre-interview

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
with one of your producers
for this show,

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:39.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Jeff Sessions resigned.
-Yeah.

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:40.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then,
we hopped off the phone

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:41.908 line:92%
and went back in it for that.

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's so much
to unpack there.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:47.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's start with Sessions,
in that he did not mention it.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:48.648 line:92%
Donald Trump did not mention it

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:51.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
during a hour and a half
press conference.

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:52.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, he was asked...
-Yes.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:54.754
-...about him very specifically.
-And yet chose --

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:57.390
But there's obviously something
he knew was happening.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is your take on this?
-Yeah.

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:00.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What are you hearing
from your sources

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:03.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
as far as was this
a forced resignation?

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:06.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
-100%, the President
asked Jeff Sessions to resign.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:08.468 size:88% position:44%
Jeff Sessions handed him
that resignation letter,

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:10.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
which said,
"You asked me to resign.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.138
Here is my resignation letter."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is not surprising.
This was expected.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:16.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
This has been rumored,
if you guys follow the news,

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:17.577 line:92%
rumored for months and months.

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:19.846
That doesn't mean it's not
still significant, right?

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a really sort of
critical moment here.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because if you look at the arc
of where Republicans were,

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:27.253
for example, back last year,
remember when Lindsey Graham,

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:30.390
the Senator, said,
"There will be holy hell to pay

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
if Donald Trump
fires Jeff Sessions."

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
Lindsey Graham
has certainly changed his tune

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
as Republicans
have come to accept, I think,

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:38.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
kind of reluctantly that
relationship is just broken.

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.033 line:92%
It's broken beyond repair.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.234 size:78% position:39%
So, what I'm hearing,
what we're hearing

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
from our team at NBC News,
is that Jeff Sessions

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
may not be gone
from the political world.

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:48.575
He's considering possibly,
per people close to him,

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:50.210
running for his old Senate seat
back in Alabama.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That Doug Jones seat.
Right.

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.146 line:92%
-Going up against Doug Jones.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:54.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he may end up
back in Washington,

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:57.650
perhaps working with or against
President Trump again.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't think he'll ever work
against President Trump.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:01.821 size:75% position:38% line:92%
That is my takeaway.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:04.190
I feel as though most
of the Republicans who've shown

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:08.194
any resistance to him ultimately
are never going to

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
truly resist anything
Donald Trump tries to do.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.265 size:84% position:42%
-The interesting thing
about Jeff Sessions is,

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:13.166 line:92%
there's a lot of headlines --

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:14.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
Listen, this all matters
as it relates --

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:15.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of it matters
as it relates

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.837 size:81% position:41%
to the Special Counsel
investigation, right?

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which Jeff Sessions
recused himself from.

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:22.008
That was, in the eyes of the
President, the original sin,

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:24.878
the thing he could never forgive
Jeff Sessions for.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:26.613 size:84% position:42%
But here's the thing --
if you look at the DOJ,

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
they've actually
implemented almost more

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.517 size:81% position:41%
than any other agency,
Donald Trump's agenda.

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:32.318
-Yeah.
-Jeff Sessions has done exactly

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:33.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
what Donald Trump
has wanted him to do.

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:35.588 size:81% position:41%
So there's this really
interesting, I think,

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:38.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
split or dichotomy
between the political sphere,

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:40.727
the political side of it,
and then the policy side.

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:44.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to ask about the fact
that Donald Trump --

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
the Russia investigation

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:46.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the reason
he fires Jeff Sessions.

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, that's a little bit
more stressful for him now

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:50.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the Democrats have taken
back the House

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:53.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they have
this power of oversight.

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:53.740 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Do you think --

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, based on
the press conference today,

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:58.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
it struck me that was a man
who was a little stressed out.

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it likely that
that's what stressing him out?

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:01.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Part of it, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:05.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Listen, for the first time,
he's now in Washington,

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:05.952 line:92%
he's inside the White House,

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:08.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he is facing
a check on his power.

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:09.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
That has not happened
for him before.

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:11.624
So, I think he's in this mode
where he's looking around,

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's what
we're hearing from folks is --

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:16.262 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's seeing,
"Hey, now Democrats do control

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.066 line:92%
the House of Representatives."

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:23.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
There will be
an onslaught of subpoenas,

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:25.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's a hassle
for West Wing staffers.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:26.573 line:92%
You have to deal with that.

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:29.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's paperwork, it's time,
it's energy,

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:31.778 size:84% position:42%
and it's also something
that Donald Trump knows

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:32.478 size:81% position:41% line:92%
is going to be coming.

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:35.014 size:84% position:42%
Now, what he did today
was issue, essentially,

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:35.882 line:92%
a threat to the Democrats.

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "Hey, I'll work with you
on infrastructure,

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:40.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll work with you on trade,
but not if you come at me

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:41.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
about my tax returns,"
for example.

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:44.791
Nancy Pelosi didn't seem so keen
on that when she spoke, so...

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:47.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well the thing I would say
why he wouldn't be keen on it,

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:48.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this is just based
on everything

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:51.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's ever said or done,
I don't believe

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:54.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he's actually
gonna be honest on that deal.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right?
Do actually see --

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think if Democrats
laid off tax returns

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:00.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
he would actually
make a deal on infrastructure?

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:00.940 line:92%
-So, here's what I can say.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a president
and this is a person --

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:06.746
and I've covered Donald Trump
for his campaign, his candidacy,

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:09.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
the transition,
the presidency now.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:10.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
He is somebody
who has issued threats

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
and not always
followed through with them,

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:13.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's just
the facts of the case.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:16.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
So there's not a lot
of past history to point to

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:18.925
that the President would
necessarily follow through

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the threat
that's he's making today.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:23.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You've been
in a lot of press conferences.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:26.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you watching today
at that mayhem,

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:29.802
and was part of you
jealous that you weren't there?

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:33.072
Or were you more super-relieved
that you were safely far away?

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:34.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God.
I was crawling out of my skin

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:37.377
making phone calls this morning
like, "I got to skip Seth.

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:38.444 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I got to go back."

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:41.614
But I had to be in New York
anyway for my MSNBC show.

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have an awesome team
at NBC News,

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:44.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so they were out there
repping NBC.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will say this, though.
Watching, and we were sort of

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:50.189
on set doing the analysis piece
for NBC News for our stations

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:52.325 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
throughout the day.

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:53.393 size:78% position:39% line:92%
There were moments --

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:55.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was tense
and uncomfortable.

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:56.696 size:81% position:41% line:92%
That's not a hot take.

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:58.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's, like,
a very lukewarm take.

00:04:58.331 --> 00:04:59.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-A press conference

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:02.702
that is not normal
for the East Room, necessarily.

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:05.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the attacks on the media
and the way that he has

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:06.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
these sort of moments
and interactions,

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:10.476
that actually does well for him
among his supporters,

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:11.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's
something to remember,

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:14.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
that that actually
plays for him.

